  "answer": "I'll look through the Shopizer storefront cart API and how store merchant configuration is read so the per-line quantity cap can be enforced without a restart.The cart writes all go through one facade. I'll enforce the store's line limit there, before anything is saved, and read the setting on each request so a change applies immediately.Virtual products that are already in the cart keep their quantity, so the cap should only apply when a request would actually change the line.A storefront cart line is now limited to the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting, or 99 when that setting is absent. The value is read on each request, so a change applies without a restart. Creating a cart or adding or changing items with a quantity above that limit returns HTTP 400 and leaves the cart unchanged. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 and an unchanged cart when a line quantity exceeds CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY, including the default of 99 and a live configuration change\"], \"missing\": [\"a storefront cart test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and calls POST /api/v1/cart, PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}, and POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi\"]}",
